{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"git rev-parse HEAD; git status --short; Get-Content docs/rubrics/decomposition-proportionality.md; rg -n -A 65 -B 4 'Decomposition proportionality inspection|Bounded abnormal inputs for the OI-85' docs/test/inspection-procedures.md; rg -n -A 20 -B 3 'id = \\\"TC-211\\\"' docs/test/test-cases.toml\"","aggregated_output":"28a03090936ffb4276d47c4accfc2f0ff119a38b\n# Rubric — decomposition proportionality (TC-211)\r\n\r\n**Adjudicates:** SR-161, SR-186. **Used by:** TC-211.\r\n\r\n**Intent:** Within the required spine, further decomposition earns its place through an independent decision or verification purpose.\r\n\r\nPass requires every R anchor and no B pattern. Record the rubric revision and cite anchor IDs. The TC and [inspection procedures](../test/inspection-procedures.md) supply the how.\r\n\r\n## Anchors\r\n\r\n**R1 — The sample is one actual completed decomposition review record whose brief presents every applicable hat's question and whose record names each applicable hat's outcome, within the required spine boundary.**\r\n\r\n**R2 — Each retained child has an independent decision or verification purpose, and the record explains why further splitting stops.**\r\n\r\n**R3 — The extra paraphrasing child with no independent purpose is reported as a finding.**\r\n\r\n**B1 — An applicable hat's outcome is missing from the review record, or prose or Hat-Refs is presented in place of the review record's outcomes.**\r\n\r\n**B2 — A paraphrasing child is accepted merely to add depth or satisfy a row-count target.**\r\n47-[P9R source review](../reviews/2026-09-06-oi85-p9r-selector-structured-opus.md)\n48-checks facade compatibility against source; the document inspector did not\n49-execute that source.\n50-\n51:## Decomposition proportionality inspection\n52-\n53-Read one actual completed decomposition review record, the declared hats roster,\n54-and the decomposition brief used by that review. Resolve the applicable hats,\n55-confirm that the brief presents every applicable hat's question and that the\n56-review record names each hat's outcome. Confirm the required spine remains the\n57-scope boundary, then inspect the complete reviewed chain and a small chain\n58-containing a child that only paraphrases or duplicates a parent's decision or\n59-verification. A missing applicable-hat outcome or a child within a required tier\n60-with no independent decision or verification purpose is an Inspection finding.\n61-Record why further splitting stops at the independent-value boundary. This\n62-procedure uses the existing brief and review record and does not impose a\n63-row-count threshold, extra depth, new record carrier, or machine coverage check.\n64-\n65:### Decomposition proportionality inspection result\n66-\n67-**PASS — 2026-10-03,** recorded as the observation\n68-`docs/test/observations/TC-211.2026-10-03T210347Z.toml`, under the procedure\n69-as it then read.\n70-\n71-**Historical INCOMPLETE — 2026-09-06, [earlier Opus 5/high Inspection](../reviews/2026-09-06-oi85-inspection-structured-opus.md).** That inspector accepted the\n72-independent purposes of SR-184/SR-185/SR-186 and their direct Inspection cases,\n73-read the stopping reason, and rejected the paraphrasing child. The procedure\n74-then required a machine-produced SR-161 perspective record that did not exist,\n75-as LLR-183 then stated. The owner ruling of 2026-09-06, re-affirmed on\n76-2026-10-13 (`docs/log.d/2026-10-25-wi976-sn036-ruling.md`), replaced that\n77-obligation with the existing hat-by-hat review path, and LLR-183 was amended\n78-accordingly. The earlier result remains incomplete for the procedure it\n79-actually executed; the ruling itself supplies no test result.\n80-\n81-## Sampled new-reader inspection\n82-\n83-A sampled observation of an assumption, not of a requirement: it can falsify\n84-DA-011, that what a random sample of the code's parts shows about its\n85-readability holds for the parts the sample did not reach. Draw five parts at\n86-random from the source the declared readability and structure measures cover,\n87-never parts their authors choose, a part being one function, class or\n88-module-level block with its own back-link. Give each to a reader who has not\n89-worked on it: a person, or a fresh model session that did not author the part,\n90-told which. The reader reads only the part's code and the records it links to,\n91-through the generated views, and states what the part does and why it exists,\n92-without asking its author. Record each statement beside the part's linked\n93-requirement and design rows, and judge whether the two agree. Sampling reads\n94-that source scope and its linked rows; re-judgement follows TC-279's declared\n95-trigger and the [observation rule](../../project-trajectory/PROCESS.md#observation-judgement).\n96-\n97-A reader who cannot say what the part does or why it exists, or whose\n98-statement contradicts the linked rows, is a failing sample and falsification\n99-evidence against DA-011, whatever the other samples show. A passing sample\n100-bounds discovery; it does not show the assumption holds for the parts it did\n101-not reach.\n102-\n103-### Sampled new-reader inspection result\n104-\n105-**PASS (sample only) — 2026-10-03, round 2, [WI-697 Claude Opus 5.5 adjudication](../reviews/wi-697-re-judge-tc-279-no-result-rec/002-ADJUDICATE-f2bc66c.md); [sample record](../reviews/wi-697-re-judge-tc-279-no-result-rec/SAMPLE-r2-f2bc66c.md).**\n106-Recorded through `record_observation.py`. This pass establishes nothing\n107-about the parts the sample did not reach.\n108-\n109-**The draw.** The population is every function, class, module-level block or\n110-module header that `gen_arch_map.declaration_sites` encloses an `Implements:`\n111-line to, under the `[paths]` roots in `docs/stack.ini`: 516 parts. The seed is\n112-trunk HEAD `f2bc66c1`, fixed by rule. One drawn key was not a part. It was a\n113-line inside a test-fixture string (`tests/test_trajectory_arch.py`\n114-`MOD_A_SRC`) naming rows that do not exist. It was skipped, and the next\n115-seeded draw was taken. That is exactly the draw the coordinator's after-the-fact\n116-live-id restriction produced. The adjudicator ruled the skip a population rule\n117-rather than a selection. It did not adopt the live-id proxy as the definition\n118-of a part.\n119-\n120-All five readers were fresh Claude Sonnet 5.5 sessions that did not author\n121-their part and were told so. Each read the part and its linked rows, from the\n122-registry files rather than the generated views, a deviation that is recorded\n123-and does not break R1.\n124-\n125-**The five statements:**\n126-\n127-- `gen_arch_map.MAPPING_FINDING_POLICY` (SR-163, LLR-276): the one declared\n128-  warn-versus-gate table, missing and stale gating, unresolved and unmapped\n129-  warning, so the burn-down needs no flag day. **Agrees.**\n130-- `session_service.KeepWarmer` (SR-227, LLR-270): a one-turn keep-warm ping\n--\n153-Its five readers all agreed with their rows. On part 3, `kitlib.spine.sn_all_ids`,\n154-one branch was misstated. Round 1 ruled that short of B1, and round 2 does not\n155-revisit it. A person may still overrule that ruling and record `fail`.\n156-\n157:## Bounded abnormal inputs for the OI-85 inspection\n158-\n159-These are synthetic counterexamples for the procedures above. They do not amend\n160-live requirements or impersonate actual reviews. The positive subjects are the\n161-real scoped amendment record and its independently logged Critique; the\n162-inspector must identify the exact versions it reads.\n163-\n164-- **Missing provenance:** verdict `APPROVE`; reviewer/session not recorded;\n165-  rubric not named; no SN/SR intent basis; no numbered anchor citations.\n166-  This one abnormal record deliberately omits all four required facts.\n167-- **Copied rubric:** a synthetic reviewer `fixture-reviewer`, session\n168-  `fixture-session`, records `APPROVE` at anchor `R1` against synthetic rubric\n169-  `fixture-rubric revision 1`. The record names SN-024 and SR-184 as intent\n170-  sources, but states that the rubric was copied verbatim from the verifying\n171-  TC-209 method without reading or independently deriving from those parents.\n172-  Every provenance slot is populated; the declared derivation is still invalid.\n173-- **Reference-only counterpart:** a synthetic change says IF-011's stale\n174-  result is now exit 2, while LLR-035/SR-168/SR-070 and callers retain the\n175-  existing behavior. Its review says only that all named IDs and endpoints\n176-  resolve and therefore the change passes. It records neither a corresponding\n177-  behavioral change nor a reason why retaining it preserves meaning.\n178-- **Missing perspective outcome:** the actual completed review record with one\n179-  applicable hat's outcome omitted, while the applicable-hat brief and all other\n180-  outcomes remain. The Inspection must identify that omitted applicable hat.\n181-- **Paraphrasing child:** the actual SR-186→TC-211 chain gains an unminted\n182-  candidate child saying “the process shall keep decomposition proportionate,”\n183-  verified by the same Inspection judgment without another decision or case.\n184-  Its only stated purpose is to make the chain look more detailed. This adds\n185-  no independent decision or verification purpose within a required tier.\n186-\n187-The historical incomplete result records what that earlier inspection examined.\n188-A later TC-211 execution inspects the actual completed review record and records\n189-its own reviewer, date, subject and findings; the owner ruling itself supplies\n190-no Inspection result.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
